Derived: g2p_en neural grapheme-to-phoneme (Apache-2.0)
-------------------------------------------------------

  g2p/js/smit-g2p.js     the loadNeuralModel / gruStep / neuralPredict trio

is a restructuring of the g2p_en GRU encoder-decoder as shipped in tiny-tts's
npm package (https://github.com/tronghieuit/tiny-tts, Apache-2.0), which is
itself a port of the g2p_en Python package. The maths — the gate order of the
GRU cell, the greedy decode, the </s> stop, the 20-step ceiling — is theirs;
the surrounding code, the vocabulary mapping and everything else here is this
project's own work.

  g2p/data/cmudict.json  CMU Pronouncing Dictionary (123,463 entries)
  g2p/data/g2p_model.json  the trained GRU weights

are data files from that Apache-2.0 package, fetched by tools/get-data.sh and
not committed. They are not distributed by this repository.


Structurally related (nothing taken)
------------------------------------

  sanoTTS (github.com/Ampixa/sanoTTS)  the project and the distillation recipe
                (docs/distillation-recipe.md upstream) whose distilled student
                stack — duration student, acoustic student, iSTFT decoder —
                this runtime implements.
  sanoTTS-jp (github.com/ayutaz/sanoTTS-jp)  the Japanese sibling of the same
                recipe, MIT-licensed. Read for how a runtime of this size
                organises a front end, porting gates and provenance notes.
                No code taken, and its weights are Japanese-only.
                (Its README cites the recipe as arXiv:2608.21378.)

The 62-symbol phoneme vocabulary, its id numbers and the model weights they
address are the *model's* input contract, not this code's. They are reproduced
here because a runtime cannot run without them; the voice weights themselves are
not part of this repository (see voices/README.md).


No espeak, no GPL
-----------------

For the avoidance of doubt, and about the code in this repository only: no part
of espeak-ng, misaki, phonemizer, piper or piper-phonemize is bundled, linked,
generated by, or derived from anything under GPL-3.0. `tools/g2p-diff.js` can
*run* the GPL front end from a vendor checkout next door to measure itself
against it, and nothing from that comparison enters the engine except a number
printed on a terminal. The voice weights are the one thing shipped with this
engine that is under GPL-3.0; they are the next section, and they are data,
unmodified, not code.


