What that means in practice:

* This repository ships **no** weight bytes. `voices/` is empty in git and
  `tools/get-data.sh voice` fetches them (see voices/README.md).
* Anyone who received weight bytes — including the packed bench page, which
  embeds them so it can run off `file://` with no network — received them under
  GPL-3.0-or-later, with this notice and the checksums above. The corresponding
  release they came from is the URL above; the GPL-3.0 text is at
  <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html>.
* The engine, the front end and the runtime are **not** subject to that licence:
  loading a GPL work into an Apache/MIT program does not make the program a
  derivative work. The two are separate works distributed side by side, and the
  engine has no GPL code in it — which is the whole point of this fork.
* The bench page prints the same attribution where the model facts are shown, so
  a page that carries the weights also carries who made them.
